From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jackwener <30525741+jackwener@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:29:10 -0400
Subject: kaze: Runtime.enable may leave console messages unreported
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A page can tell that a debugger is attached: once Runtime.enable is on, V8
serializes every console.log argument for the client, which runs the getters
of the logged objects (an Error's stack, say) — the classic CDP detection.
Kaze's agent drives pages over CDP, so sites that look for it (BOSS直聘)
closed themselves the moment it began.

Ported from OpenBrowser's 004-session-console-reporting: Runtime.enable takes
two experimental options, reportConsoleMessages and serializeConsoleObjects
(both true by default, so DevTools is unchanged). An automation client that
passes false gets execution contexts and evaluation as before, but console
messages and exceptions are not serialized: no getter of the page's runs.
